(* ==========================================================================
   tuonelang grammar

   THE FORMAL SURFACE GRAMMAR IS NOT YET WRITTEN.

   Status (see CONSTITUTION.md): tuonelang's v0 *semantics* are now frozen, and
   several surface-syntax elements are decided at the level of illustrative
   examples (braces + semicolons, `let`/`var`/`const`, `fn`, `struct`, `enum`,
   `interface`/`impl`, `match`, bracketed generics `[T]`, parameter modes
   `in`/`mut`/`take`, `spec`). However, the *authoritative* EBNF productions
   have deliberately NOT been transcribed here yet.

   Why this file is still a placeholder:
     - Some surface forms are explicitly marked Experimental in the Constitution
       (e.g. the `given`/`when`/`then` spec syntax §27, the dynamic-dispatch
       spelling §19, labeled-loop sigils §16). Writing them into a normative
       grammar now would imply a stability the Constitution does not yet claim.
     - The grammar must be derived from, and kept in lockstep with, the lexer
       (tuo-lexer) and parser (tuo-parser). Authoring it before those exist
       risks a grammar that silently diverges from the implementation.

   When the grammar is written it will:
     - be normative EBNF, cross-referenced to CONSTITUTION.md section numbers;
     - cover exactly the Frozen surface forms, marking Experimental productions
       as such;
     - stay in sync with tuo-lexer / tuo-parser and be checked against them.

   Until then, the CONSTITUTION.md examples are illustrative, not normative, and
   this file intentionally contains no productions.
   ========================================================================== *)
